Wycheproof vectors are from C2SP/wycheproof commit
3fa63dd0344abb611f1fb1d77e119938603ea230, under Apache-2.0; see
 tests/data/WYCHEPROOF-LICENSE.txt. Vector values and verdicts are preserved
except for explicit malformed-input classification at the Rust API's bounds.

The context-binding fixture uses a public deterministic test seed. It was
created with the same native backend and is not an independent crypto reference.
Detailed import hashes, corpus generation and test evidence are maintained at
https://github.com/tosnetwork/memo/tree/main/rtos.

Falcon-512 padded verification uses the official Falcon-impl-20211101 source
archive (SHA-256 d9f982bd825b9903b57b686d6d26018dac173a1dff09f224cc39302f9d85a595),
as vendored by tosnetwork/tos at the fixed revision above. The selected
codec/common/shake/vrfy sources and headers are unmodified MIT-licensed copies;
see native/falcon-reference/LICENSE and the source headers. Only verification
code is compiled; signing, key generation, RNG and floating-point code are not
linked. The fixed-profile adapter adapts crypto/pq/falcon512-native.c with an
RTOS symbol namespace. This is original Falcon, not FN-DSA or FIPS certification.

The Falcon fixtures extract the 100 published Falcon-512 round-3 KAT answers
(SHA-256 dd75c946fdedef4ec46a2bee7e10c65c9126f1a839b9ced6921fd45f7354b5cd).
RTOS converted signed-message framing to detached signatures, padded to 666
bytes with zeroes, and added message mutation controls. Coefficients and
nonces are unchanged. The original submission and source are MIT licensed
(see native/falcon-reference/LICENSE). An additional 28 fixed-profile cases
come from the pinned reference test/pq-falcon512/vectors.json; its GPLv3
license text is retained at tests/data/TOS-LICENSE.txt.
